  "Shutdown.PowerOffOption": "Turn off the device when closing the application",
  "Shutdown.PowerOffHint": "Off by default. On an actual exit from Yamahama, reads the connected device state and turns it off if it is on. Hiding in the tray or closing Settings does not turn off the device. Does not connect to another device. Forced process termination or Bluetooth loss may prevent the command from completing.",
  "PowerProtection.Enable": "Prevent the device from turning off",
  "PowerProtection.Hint": "Off by default. Protection starts after power-on is read in the current connection. Yamahama checks the state about every 15 seconds, including while in the tray, and turns the device back on after confirmed standby. It does not turn on a device that was already off when connected. After an error it waits at least 60 seconds before retrying. It does not reconnect a lost connection.",
  "PowerProtection.SafetyName": "Important information about power protection",
  "PowerProtection.Safety": "Bluetooth does not report why power was turned off. Protection also reacts to switching off with the remote, touch panel or this application. Disable this option to leave the soundbar in standby. It requires the application to be running, an active Bluetooth connection and an awake computer; it does not change the soundbar's auto-standby setting.",
  "PowerProtection.Saved": "Power protection preference saved.",
  "PowerProtection.Restored": "Power protection: the soundbar has confirmed that it is on again.",
  "PowerProtection.NotConfirmed": "The soundbar did not confirm power-on.",
  "PowerProtection.Failed": "Power protection failed. Another attempt will be made no sooner than 60 seconds later if the connection remains active. ",
  "PowerProtection.Cancelled": "Automatic soundbar power-on was cancelled. ",
