  "Tabs.Settings": "Settings",
  "Tabs.SettingsName": "Application settings",
  "Settings.AutoApply": "Apply input, sound mode and indicator brightness selections immediately",
  "Settings.AutoApplyName": "Automatically apply input, sound mode and indicator brightness selections",
  "Settings.AutoApplyHint": "After confirming settings with OK, disabling this option enables Apply buttons. Changing the option does not send earlier selections to the soundbar.",
  "Settings.ShowHints": "Show hints and helpful descriptions",
  "Settings.ShowHintsName": "Show hints and helpful descriptions, including for screen readers",
  "Settings.ShowHintsHint": "After confirming with OK, turns off optional on-screen descriptions and screen reader help, including the Application sections and Settings categories tab-group names. Individual tab and control names, readings, errors and help opened on request remain available.",
  "Settings.AutoApplyExplanation": "Immediate application covers input, sound mode and indicator brightness lists on the Soundbar control tab. Sound checkboxes and −/+ buttons send changes when pressed. Only a soundbar response confirms success. Preferences in the Settings window require OK and are not hardware commands.",
  "Settings.HintsExplanation": "Disabling usage hints also hides the optional Application sections and Settings categories tab-group names, but not individual tab names, essential labels, errors or connection state. Operation messages and screen-reader state announcements have separate settings. Help and Firmware remain available when explicitly opened.",
  "Settings.RememberingName": "Remembering connections",
  "Tabs.Help": "Help",
  "Tabs.HelpName": "Help and requirements",
  "Help.Label": "About and requirements:",
  "Help.Name": "Help: unofficial remote, Bluetooth BLE and .NET Desktop Runtime 10",
  "Help.Hint": "You can read the text with the arrow keys and copy it. Open the official manual with the button below the text.",
  "Help.OpenManual": "Open the official Yamaha SR-C30A manual",
  "Help.OpenManualName": "Open the official Yamaha SR-C30A manual in a browser",
  "Help.OpenManualHint": "Requires Internet access. Opens manual.yamaha.com.",
  "Guide.TouchPanelLabel": "Touch panel lock and supported features:",
  "Guide.TouchPanelName": "Child Lock touch panel guide and feature coverage",
  "Guide.TouchPanelHint": "Offline guide. Change the lock with the remote as instructed. The application does not send lock commands and does not know the lock state. You can read with the arrow keys and copy the text.",
  "Help.AppearanceName": "Application settings, saving and closing",
  "Status.Label": "Message:",
  "Status.Ready": "Ready. Choose Search to find your soundbar.",
  "Status.Name": "Operation message",
  "Status.Hint": "Result of the last operation. An error moves focus to this field. Background reading updates do not change focus.",
  "Control.Refresh": "_Refresh",
  "Control.RefreshName": "Refresh the actual device state",
  "Control.Cancel": "_Cancel operation",
  "Control.CancelName": "Cancel the current operation",
  "Control.CancelHint": "Cancellation does not undo a command that the soundbar may already have received.",
  "Settings.Remembering": "Connect and save remembers a name and address after verifying model and state. Select a saved entry to connect without scanning. File → Connect once does not add the device. Add device saves the connected soundbar; Remove saved device removes only a local record. The application does not change Windows audio pairing. Startup connection-only is on by default; the separate startup power-on option is off by default. Scan again if the BLE address changes.",
  "Help.Overview": "Yamahama — test release. Reading the real device has been verified; every physical command effect has not yet been confirmed.\n\nYamahama — unofficial Yamaha SR-C30A soundbar remote for Windows.\nThe application is not a Yamaha product or a tool approved by Yamaha. The Yamaha, Clear Voice and Bass Extension names belong to their respective owners.\n\nConnection requires an adapter and driver supporting Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE), Bluetooth enabled, and a soundbar within range. BLE control does not transmit audio or select the Windows audio output. Simultaneous phone and computer control is not guaranteed. If problems occur, close the control application on your phone and try again.\n\nFirst choose Search, select a device from the list and choose Connect. On the Soundbar control tab, checkboxes change a setting when pressed and lists apply selections immediately by default. In Settings, you can turn off immediate application and use Apply buttons. Only the device response confirms success. After an error or cancellation, a command may already have reached the soundbar — use Refresh to check the actual state.\n\n.NET Desktop Runtime 10 matching the application's architecture is required. The application is intended for framework-dependent publishing without a bundled .NET runtime. The native .exe uses the standard .NET host dialog offering to download the missing runtime.\n\nKeyboard controls: Tab and Shift+Tab — next and previous control or visible readout. Enter a profile list or a saved or discovered device list with one Tab press; arrow keys immediately select its items, without an extra Tab. The next Tab leaves the list. Enter or Space activates a button. Open menus with Alt, not Tab; Alt with the underlined letter activates an access key, and Ctrl+Tab changes tabs. Ctrl with plus/minus changes volume; Alt with plus/minus changes subwoofer gain. Numeric keypad plus/minus keys also work. The −/+ buttons adjust volume and subwoofer immediately, without another confirmation step.\n\nIn first-run setup and Settings, Current value display has three choices: Read-only fields, Static text (the default) and None. None hides only duplicated parameter readouts; it does not remove essential control names and states, connection and power state, errors or warnings. Operation messages and confirmed-state announcements can be enabled independently. Standard NVDA control-name and state feedback is independent of these settings. Background updates do not move focus. Full NVDA speech and high-contrast validation remain unconfirmed.\n\nThe manual opens only on your request, in the default browser. Firmware help is available offline too. The Bluetooth adapter guide and full manufacturer PDF are separate project-folder files, not part of the application. The application does not install firmware or provide CEC or an EQ.\n\nSliders are the default for volume and subwoofer gain; buttons remain available in File → Settings. The main window contains the Soundbar control and Devices tabs; other views open from menus. The optional Application sections and Settings categories tab-group names disappear when hints are disabled; individual tab names remain available.\n\nFile → Settings has six topic tabs. Changes remain a draft with no live preview: save and apply with OK or discard with Cancel. Independent profile and soundbar operations are not undone. Details of saving, reset and closing, plus safety information, appear later in this Help view.",
  "Help.Appearance": "File → Settings opens six tabs: Appearance (language, theme and text size), Main screen (nine visibility settings), Controls and feedback (sliders or buttons, hints, messages and readouts), Startup and power (Windows startup, startup device, automatic connection, startup power-on and power protection), Closing (device power-off when closing the application, tray hiding and an exit warning), and Profiles and application defaults. Arrow keys switch tabs while a header has focus; Ctrl+Tab switches tabs, and Tab enters their content.\n\nPreference changes remain a draft until OK. Before OK they do not change language, theme, text size, visibility or application behavior and are not saved. Cancel, Escape or closing Settings discards unsaved changes after confirmation if anything was changed. A save failure keeps the window open for retry. Each of the first five tabs has a Restore default settings button: its confirmation identifies the current tab, the reset affects only that tab’s preferences and it waits for OK. Other tabs, the language, saved devices and profiles remain unchanged. Resetting Appearance affects theme and text size; restore visibility on the Main screen tab. The identically named button on Profiles and application defaults affects the whole application and has a separate confirmation of that scope. It preserves language, completed first-run setup, devices and profiles; it does not reopen setup. Profile and device actions are independent and are not undone by Cancel. Reset guides are in the Help menu and send no hardware commands.\n\nThere is no separate Theme menu. Windows high-contrast mode takes priority. Hiding a row does not change soundbar settings. config.json and the langs folder with pl.lng and en.lng belong beside the EXE; the application folder must be writable. Clearing a session does not remove saved devices, and removing a saved entry does not change Windows pairing.\n\nThe main window contains Soundbar control and Devices tabs. With tray hiding enabled, closing the main window, including X, Alt+F4 and Close in the Windows system menu, hides it instead of exiting. Explicit File → Exit and Exit Yamahama in the tray icon menu still exit. Warn before closing the application is on by default; disable it on the Closing tab and confirm with OK if desired. Hiding the window or closing an auxiliary window does not ask to exit or trigger soundbar power-off. Escape does not exit the application. Automatic-connection and power-protection safety information is in Help, including when hints are disabled. The Exit dialog asks a short question; its extra explanation appears only when hints are enabled.",
